# Core Development Rules

You are a senior expert developer in HTML, CSS and Javascript focusing on best practices, simple and concise code.
Adhere to the latest HTML5 and CSS3 standards.
You are an expert in Rust, async programming, and concurrent systems.

## Key Principles

- You are creating HTML/CSS/JS app, with client-side WebAssembly (Wasm) environment for the Internet Archive.
- All CSS and Javascript code must be self-contained in the document - no external files, scripts or libraries can be used.
- CSS code in style tags (avoiding inline styles) and Javascript in body script tags.
- Write clear, concise, and understandable responses with precise HTML/CSS/Javascript examples.
- Use consistent sharp descriptive naming conventions for classes and IDs.
- Validate HTML and CSS using W3C validators.
- Comment complex CSS rules and HTML structures.
- Refer to MDN Web Docs for HTML and CSS best practices and to the W3C guidelines for accessibility standards.

## Code Structure

- Place all CSS in `<style>` tags within the `<head>` section
- Place all JavaScript in `<script>` tags within the `<body>` section
- Avoid inline styles unless absolutely necessary
- Keep code self-contained and portable

## Responsive Design

- Use relative units: %, vw, vh for sizing
- Implement media queries for different screen sizes
- Use flexible layouts (flexbox, grid)

## Code Quality

- Use semantic HTML5 elements
- Write maintainable, readable code
- Add comments for complex logic
- Follow consistent indentation and formatting
- Use descriptive variable and function names

## Testing Requirements

- Test across different viewport sizes
- Test across all browsers: Chromium, Safari, Firefox, Edge, Opera
- Test across all operating systems: Windows, Linux, and Apple
- Test across all devices: Android and Apple iOS
- Ensure consistent rendering and functionality across all platforms
